course: dictionary
lesson: 5021
title: Formal and informal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Informal means relaxed and friendly, not following strict rules. «Diaries often use informal language and contractions such as I'm, can't and didn't.» A diary is private, so the writer can relax, and short forms like I'm and can't sound more like speaking. Informal is the opposite of formal, which is careful and polite.
explain: Informal can also mean not official. «An informal agreement» is made between friends, perhaps with a handshake, and is not written into a formal contract. Clue words help you spot it: party, chat and clothes all suggest a relaxed, everyday situation.
explain: Choosing your style is a skill. You talk informally to mates and family, but formally to teachers and strangers. Ask yourself who you are writing to and how relaxed the moment is, then match your words to that person.
fact: Informal means relaxed and friendly, not following strict rules.
fact: «Informal language» is the everyday way people talk to friends and family.
fact: Words like «gonna», «kids» and «mate» are informal, so they would not usually appear in a formal letter.
fact: «Informal» can also mean not official, as in «an informal agreement».
fact: The style you choose for speaking or writing is called your register.
exercise: «Her party was informal, so everyone wore jeans and sat on the floor.» What does informal mean here? | *Relaxed and friendly, not strict | Very expensive and grand | Cold and silent | Written down in a formal letter
exercise: Which sentence uses informal language? | Yours faithfully, the Board of Governors. | Dear Headteacher, I am writing to request a meeting. | Please find enclosed the form as requested. | *Hi mate, gonna be late, see you in a bit.
exercise: «An informal agreement» is one that is... | Read out loud in assembly | *Not official, made between friends | Printed in a newspaper | Written and signed by a judge
test: Which letter is informal? | A complaint letter to a shop manager | A letter to the head teacher asking for a day off | A letter to the council about a broken bin | *A letter to your best friend about your weekend
test: Diaries often use contractions. Which one is a contraction? | canned | cannot | *can't | could
exam: Which sentence shows an informal register? | Please find attached the report as requested. | Dear Ms Patel, I am writing to inform you of a delay. | I respectfully request an extension to the deadline. | *Hiya, I'm gonna be late
